    <Label Name="Title" Style="GalleryTitle" Text="Circle in a square touching two arcs" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="208" WrapWidth="538.5" Backdrop="true" />
    <Label Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="Let P be the blue circle’s center and r its radius. Let M be the midpoint of AD, the center of the purple semicircle, and let N be the foot of the perpendicular from P to AD, so AN = r and NP = x.\n\nThe blue circle touches the red quarter circle from inside, so AP = 8 − r. It touches the purple semicircle from outside, so MP = 4 + r.\n\nIn triangle ANP, with the right angle at N, x² = AP² − AN² = (8 − r)² − r² = 64 − 16r. In triangle MNP, with the right angle at N and MN = 4 − r, x² = MP² − MN² = (4 + r)² − (4 − r)² = 16r.\n\nSetting them equal gives r = 2 and x = 4√2, so AP = MP = 6 and N is the midpoint of AM. That is how P was constructed: on the dashed perpendicular to AD through N, 6 away from A." Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="252.5" WrapWidth="538.5" Backdrop="true" />
    <Segment Name="x" Style="CoincidentLine">
      <Dependency Name="N" />
      <Dependency Name="P" />
    </Segment>
    <FigureLabel Name="FigureLabel2" OffsetX="-6.499999999592319" OffsetY="-25.00000000083844">
      <Dependency Name="x" />
    </FigureLabel>
